  "limitations": [
    "Controlled committed-prefix reopening is not an OS crash or distributed handoff test",
    "Child metadata costs isolate the real loader with a controlled active-view port; not full child boot cost",
    "Short deliberate waits establish cancellation/budget boundaries, not an observed infinite outage",
    "Single-image read uses a 1x1 PNG and proves duplicate object reads, not large-image model timeout causality",
    "Prior live large-image cold recall remains unaccepted",
    "The original constant SQL-count context sample varied old Entries only; it did not cover completed Submission growth. Comparison index exists only in the disposable fixture.",
    "Family timing uses fresh short-text children, pre-granted authority and synchronous PG projection instead of Kafka. Native host is cold; PG caches may be warm from seeding. No full failover SLA, large-context or fleet-capacity claim."
